# Security Rules
- NEVER attempt to read or modify .env or .env.local files.
- NEVER output live secret keys, passwords, or tokens in chat responses.
- If an environment variable needs to be updated or added, instruct the user to use the Vercel CLI via 'vercel env add' or the Vercel Web Dashboard.

# Research / prototype phase (not a business)
- GRYPS is a non-commercial R&D / portfolio prototype. Do not add monetization or commercial go-to-market in this phase.
- Explicitly deferred (internal project control — do not publish as a public “deferred commercial” table): payments, subscriptions, customer billing, sales CRM, commercial lead capture, customer contracts, paid reports, customer onboarding, team collaboration, commercial API, marketplace, advertising.
- Prefer language: Research · Prototype · Experimental · Assessment · Methodology · Evidence · Scenario · Intelligence.
- Avoid language: “Buy” · “Get a quote” · “For customers” · “Our solution” · “Book a consultation” · “Enterprise plans” (and similar sales/customer phrasing).
- Canonical CTA remains Generate Resilience Signature — never freemium, trial, or pricing-ladder CTAs.
- Public posture page: `/research-prototype` (product-facing only). Do not publish career objectives (“Can Henrique independently…”) or personal administrative / unemployment-benefit notes in the GRYPS UI.
- Separation: product UI = research prototype; `/case-study` = portfolio demonstration; personal project-control notes (full sprint rationale, benefit context) stay outside the public product (e.g. private Notion).

# Typography — dashes (EN + FI user-facing copy)
- Hyphen `-` (U+002D): compounds, prefixes, IDs (`non-commercial`, `safety-critical`, `deterministic-v0.3`). Finnish open-compound attachments keep a space before the hyphen (`Signature -pisteet`).
- En dash `–` (U+2013): ranges and spans (`0–100`, `55–85°`, `75–89`, `LEO–MEO–GEO`, `~20–50ms`). Never ASCII hyphen for ranges.
- Em dash `—` (U+2014): prose breaks and contrasts (`…risk — not certification`), page `<title>` pairs (`Methodology — How…`). Prefer one em dash per sentence.
- Minus `−` (U+2212): negative quantities (`−30°C`, `lng −30–40°`).
- Middle dot `·` (U+00B7): UI chrome only — CTAs, chips, meta stacks, ALL-CAPS labels (`Score my site · free`, `OPS CONSOLE · EXAMPLE SITES`). Do not use em dash for those short qualifiers.
- Empty / null display: em dash `—` alone is fine.
- Code comments may keep em dashes; do not “fix” math operators (`a - b`).
